17.
RESOLUTION
— Directing the Planning Department to review the Unified Development
Code and provide a recommendation to the Governing Body regarding the allowance of a
greater variety of trees
and
smaller
tree
sizes
in
new residential
developments.
(SPONSORS
- DR. ALDRICH, MR. ESQUIBEL, MR. MOODY, MR. ROYBAL AND
MR. WHITE)
Mr. White moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Dr. Aldrich, sponsor of the item, provided information regarding the proposed resolution including
numerous complaints and concerns associated with requirements for trees in the Unified
Development Code.
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Department Director, provided
background infonnation related to required trees by development type and provided various
examples. Mark Ellison. Urban Forestry Manager, provided a presentation which included various
examples of both shade and ornamental trees on varying lot sizes and noted the advantages of
shade trees.
Chairman Segrave and all committee members commented on the item.
Public
comments were made by Jeannie Andcrson-Shrednik. Parks and Greenway Planner; Phillip
Bowling, Cheyenne Board of Realtors; Mark Ernste. Tank House Nursery; Jeff Geyer; Jeremey
llamilton. #1 Properties: Nancy Loomis; and Ben Rayl, #1 Properties.
